      "message": "Looking into its handler, `bluetooth_gatt.lock().unwrap().enable(false)` call is necessary to avoid other crashes.\n\nAlso, without the `self.intf.lock().unwrap().disable()` call I\u0027m afraid of the LibBluetooth threads would be aborted in an unexpected point and cause other crashes (something like throw_system_error from recursive_mutex).\n\nI think we should only skip the discoverable/connectable calls. Perhaps we could even decouple `APIMessage::ShutDown` and `Message::AdapterShutdown`, that is, sending `Message::AdapterShutdown` from the signal handler rather than here.",
